# Design Sources Registry

Spec: DesignSources
Purpose:
  Registry of design inspiration/pattern sources with extraction status.
  Makes the system AWARE which sources' design skills are obtained vs not,
  per user requirement ("AI bilsin hansı saytların design skilləri hələ
  alınmayıb"). Legality: LEARN patterns/principles — NEVER copy assets.

Owns: design/sources.sdd

Research basis: r4-design-sources (2026-09-06) — citations in
  @../../docs/analysis/ai-agents-comparative.md section 5

Sources:
  # === Layer 1: machine-readable design systems (foundation) ===
  material_design_3:
    url: https://m3.material.io
    type: full design system
    machine_readable: YES (Design System Package DSP + Figma kit)
    extractable: token architecture (reference/secondary/component tiers),
      HCT dynamic color, tonal elevation, shape/motion scales, component specs
    status: EXTRACTED (default vocabulary for design/intelligence/ module)
    license: openly documented; attribute Material Design
  carbon:
    url: https://carbondesignsystem.com
    type: full design system (enterprise)
    machine_readable: YES (TS token objects, stylelint plugin, Figma v11)
    extractable: data tables, filters, complex forms, ~200 tokens/theme,
      Carbon Charts dataviz, 2x-grid, accessibility rigor
    status: EXTRACTED (enterprise/UI-density reference)
    license: Apache-2.0 code; attribute Carbon
  polaris:
    url: https://polaris.shopify.com
    type: full design system (commerce/admin)
    machine_readable: YES (polaris-tokens npm, MIT: JS/JSON/CSS/SCSS)
    extractable: content+pattern pairing (UX writing as first-class),
      semantic color naming grammar, merchant task flows
    status: EXTRACTED (UX-writing + commerce patterns)
    license: MIT tokens; attribute Polaris
  fluent_2:
    url: https://fluent2.microsoft.design
    type: full design system (cross-platform)
    machine_readable: YES (DesignToken TS API → CSS custom properties)
    extractable: density-aware adaptive tokens (compact/comfortable),
      cross-platform portability
    status: EXTRACTED (density adaptation pattern)
    license: MIT code; attribute Fluent
  apple_hig:
    url: https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/
    type: platform guidelines
    machine_readable: PARTIAL (community mirrors: apple-hig GitHub catalog)
    extractable: platform conventions, materials, Dynamic Type, SF Symbols,
      hit targets >= 44pt, clarity/deference philosophy
    status: EXTRACTED (platform constraint loading)
    license: guidelines open; assets license-restricted
  # === Layer 2: agent-native / flow libraries ===
  refero:
    url: https://refero.design
    type: real-product research library + MCP server
    machine_readable: YES (MCP, search-by-image, DESIGN.md exports)
    extractable: real web/iOS screens by page type/flow/pattern;
      agent-native reference lookup
    status: EXTRACTED (priority — only gallery with MCP; pattern-lookup stage)
    license: DESIGN.md exports agent-consumable; do not scrape screens
  mobbin:
    url: https://mobbin.com
    type: real-app screenshot library (1,400+ apps, 620k+ screens, 320k+ flows)
    machine_readable: PARTIAL (search index, Figma plugin, OCR)
    extractable: shipped-product flows (onboarding, paywall, checkout, empty
      states), UI element conventions
    status: EXTRACTED (workflow: study 5-10 real flows → abstract textual
      pattern cards — store descriptions, not images)
    license: subscription access; LEARN flows; never republish
  # === Layer 3: judgment / rubrics ===
  awwwards:
    url: https://www.awwwards.com
    type: juried gallery
    machine_readable: NO
    extractable: explicit jury rubric — Design 40 / Usability 30 /
      Creativity 20 / Content 10; avant-garde layouts; motion
    status: EXTRACTED (rubric internalized as evaluation checklist)
    license: criteria are facts, freely referenceable; do not clone sites
  anti_slop_canon:
    url: github.com/Nutlope/hallmark + smoothui.dev + docs.bswen.com
    type: 2026 anti-slop literature
    machine_readable: N/A (methodology)
    extractable: 57 slop-test gates; closed-loop build→critique→fix;
      grading framework (originality 40%)
    status: EXTRACTED (encoded in design/intelligence/ rules)
    license: Hallmark MIT
  # === Layer 4: style-direction galleries (reference layer) ===
  dribbble:
    url: https://dribbble.com
    type: designer showcase (concept shots)
    extractable: trend vocabulary (textual summaries only)
    status: REFERENCE (style-trend analysis; images never stored)
  godly_website:
    url: https://godly.website
    type: curated top-1% landing gallery
    extractable: current landing aesthetics direction cards
    status: REFERENCE
  land_book:
    url: https://land-book.com
    type: gallery with style/industry taxonomy
    extractable: landing archetypes per industry
    status: REFERENCE
  lapa_ninja:
    url: https://www.lapa.ninja
    type: landing-page gallery (7,300+)
    extractable: section anatomy recipes (structural, not visual)
    status: REFERENCE
  siteinspire:
    url: https://www.siteinspire.com
    type: fine/editorial gallery
    extractable: layout grammar (typographic, grid, unusual)
    status: REFERENCE
  httpster:
    url: https://httpster.net
    type: type-led/brutalist gallery
    extractable: anti-generic counter-aesthetic directions
    status: REFERENCE (anti-slop escape hatch)
  dark_mode_design:
    url: https://www.darkmodedesign.com
    type: dark-mode gallery
    extractable: dark-surface hierarchy constraint set
    status: REFERENCE
  figma_community:
    url: https://www.figma.com/community
    type: public UI kits + variables
    machine_readable: YES (DTCG JSON export via plugins)
    extractable: component architecture, token naming conventions
    status: EXTRACTED (license-check workflow defined — see below)
    license_check_workflow:
      - Every Community file carries its own license (many CC BY; Apple/Google
        kits free but under their terms)
      - BEFORE extracting a kit: open file page, read license field, record
        license in the extract's INDEX.sdd provenance
      - CC BY / CC0 kits: token structure and naming extractable WITH attribution
      - Vendor kits (Apple/Google/IBM): structure learning only — tokens
        reference the vendor system, never re-published as SDDRA's own
      - Unlicensed/ambiguous: SKIP, mark REFERENCE
  behance:
    url: https://www.behance.net
    type: portfolio case studies
    extractable: case-study structure, design rationale
    status: REFERENCE
  patterns_dev:
    url: https://www.patterns.dev
    type: implementation pattern catalog (free book)
    machine_readable: YES (code examples)
    extractable: React/UI patterns, AI UI patterns (streaming, traces)
    status: EXTRACTED 2026-09-07 (25 patterns + AI UI chapter detail)
    extract: @imported/patterns-dev-extract.sdd
  design_notes:
    url: https://design-notes.show
    type: design philosophy podcast
    extractable: principles behind design systems (transcripts)
    status: PLANNED (deferred — principle distillation lower priority than
      implementation layer; revisit when design intelligence needs
      philosophy-layer grounding)

ExtractionRoadmap (priority order):
  1. material_design_3 — vocabulary (DONE: module default tokens)
  2. refero — agent-native lookup (DONE: pattern-lookup stage)
  3. awwwards + anti_slop_canon — judgment (DONE: rubric + gates)
  4. mobbin — real-flow patterns (DONE: textual pattern-card workflow)
  5. carbon — enterprise density (DONE: reference)
  6. polaris — UX writing (DONE: reference)
  7. figma_community + patterns_dev — implementation layer (DONE 2026-09-07:
     patterns_dev extracted via imported/patterns-dev-extract.sdd; figma
     license-check workflow defined)
  8. style galleries — direction layer (as-needed per project brief)
  9. design_notes — philosophy layer (DEFERRED)

Rules:
  [DSRC1] LEARN patterns/principles/tokens — NEVER copy assets, logos,
          copyrighted visuals. Gallery screenshots are never stored in .sdd/.
  [DSRC2] Machine-readable tokens (M3/Polaris/Carbon/Fluent) referenced WITH
          attribution; never presented as SDDRA's own.
  [DSRC3] Status transitions: REFERENCE → PLANNED → EXTRACTED (append-only
          history; never downgrade silently).
  [DSRC4] New sources require a weak-point-map or module justification.
  [DSRC5] Refero MCP usage requires user credentials — never scraped.

Navigation:
